WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.570
An autumn night in Amritsar.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:06.690
Lamps glow around a golden
building standing in a pool.

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.910
Hindu families light lamps
at this time of year too.

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.980
Many remember Rama's return to Ayodhya.

5
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.750
But many Sikhs tell a different story.

6
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.190
It begins with a Guru held in
Gwalior Fort by a Mughal emperor.

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.050
So why would Sikhs light up their most
famous temple to remember a Guru walking

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.390
out of prison?

9
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.000
In this mission, you'll meet the gurpurbs:

10
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.260
days marking the Gurus'
births and martyrdoms.

11
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.670
Then you'll see how these festivals
look in Punjab and in Britain.

12
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.030
Your mission: find out why a Guru's walk
out of prison is celebrated with light.
